		{
			"id": "115939713096417230",
			"parentId": "115939690969223339",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/115939713096417230",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-01-22T16:33:46.105Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://typo.social/@TiroTypeworks\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>TiroTypeworks</span></a></span> this perspective doesn’t resonate with me, knowing my incentives and internal motivations as a maintainer (not an “external” contributor) but I am curious what you mean!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115939770543176750",
			"parentId": "115939713096417230",
			"url": "https://typo.social/@TiroTypeworks/115939770517724800",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tiro Typeworks",
				"url": "https://typo.social/@TiroTypeworks",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/303/361/125/488/813/original/20f24bfe48467c56.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2026-01-22T16:48:22.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> There’s this notion in FOSS, which I have heard from numerous people over the years, that open software/font development is a service industry, so you make a thing, release it under an open license, and then customers come along and pay you to extend, modify, or customise it.</p><p>I’ve seen a lot of unfunded work done in that ‘make a thing’ phase. In some respects, this isn’t very different from any speculative development, except you’ve given away the thing that is most easily monetised, i.e. the rights, in the hope that a customer needs something a bit different and will pay you, rather than anyone else on the planet, to modify what you made.</p><p>[To be clear, I like FOSS, but development needs to be funded.]</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115939793921567088",
			"parentId": "115939770543176750",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/115939793921567088",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-01-22T16:54:19.399Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://typo.social/@TiroTypeworks\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>TiroTypeworks</span></a></span> a ha, yes — that gives me a lot more detail and makes a lot more sense: thank you!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115939806740337190",
			"parentId": "115939793921567088",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/115939806740337190",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-01-22T16:57:34.998Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://typo.social/@TiroTypeworks\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>TiroTypeworks</span></a></span> The other wrinkle I think about a lot is how GIANT megacorps or investors can fund a free or near-free service at a loss to completely change the incentives of customers to be less friendly to existing creators trying to succeed sustainably in the same space.</p><p>Reminds me of Walmart/Amazon decimating the economy of small towns</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "115939933855599105",
			"parentId": "115939806740337190",
			"url": "https://typo.social/@TiroTypeworks/115939933826642097",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tiro Typeworks",
				"url": "https://typo.social/@TiroTypeworks",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/303/361/125/488/813/original/20f24bfe48467c56.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2026-01-22T17:29:54.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I’ve tried to describe this, in conversations with free software fundamentalists, in terms of disparity in ability to leverage value. What you describe is a particularly brutal way to leverage value from FOSS, but it is part of the larger issue that is simply stated as ‘Capital can leverage value at a scale and in ways that lack of capital can’t’. So when I release a font under OFL, I am aware that I am giving something to users — yay! —but I am also providing exploitable value to capital — boo!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		}
